v0.10.23: legacy-slugs perf — N+1 → 1 + GIN index on agents_used

Ivan hit this running the v0.10.20 audit tool:

  $ abw admin agents legacy-slugs
  error: operation timed out (60s)

The v0.10.20 handler was correct but slow. Two problems stacked:

1. N+1 JSONB queries: one COUNT per legacy name, ~43 sequential.
2. No GIN index on fermi_forecasts.agents_used — every containment
   query seq-scanned the whole table.

43 × seq-scan >> 60s reqwest timeout. Request never completed.

(v0.10.21/v0.10.22 were parallel forecast-save fixes — simulation
persistence and confidence-interval clamping. Unrelated to this
hotfix.)

Fixes:

Migration 168 — CREATE INDEX ... USING gin(agents_used).
Idempotent, PgBouncer-safe, no CONCURRENTLY (can't run inside a
tx, and the table is small enough that the exclusive lock is
sub-second). Registered in run_migrations().

Handler rewrite — src/handlers/admin.rs::admin_legacy_agent_slugs_handler.
Replaced the per-name COUNT loop with one query:

  SELECT ln.name, COUNT(f.id)::int8 AS refs
    FROM unnest($1::text[]) AS ln(name)
    LEFT JOIN fermi_forecasts f
           ON f.agents_used @> jsonb_build_array(
                jsonb_build_object('agent_name', ln.name))
   GROUP BY ln.name

LEFT JOIN preserves zero-ref names. Bound $1 = the array of all
legacy names. One round trip, one seq-scan (or fast GIN lookups
post-mig-168).

Combined effect: audit endpoint returns in milliseconds instead
of timing out.

Other read sites that get faster for free (same GIN index):
  * handlers/eval_brier.rs (Brier lookup by agent_name)
  * handlers/agents.rs::get_agent_calibration_handler
  * handlers/forecasts.rs::loop_health_handler

No client timeout bump — a well-connected request that can't
complete in 60s is a server perf issue, not a client-timeout
issue. Fixed at the right layer.

Post-deploy:
  psql -c "\d public.fermi_forecasts" | grep agents_used_gin
  time curl -s $URL/api/admin/agents/legacy-slugs | jq .total_legacy
  abw admin agents legacy-slugs

